No records were truly kept before Sokoban, which was the first branch
of the Dungeon completed by Erik the male human chaotic ranger, after
approximately 8000 minutes of exploration.  At this point, he'd
gathered several rings, wands, and scrolls (all unidentified), a bag
of holding, and a suit of armor bringing his armor class down to -4.
The only remarkable piece included was a dwarvish mithril coat.  It's
known that he prayed once, after a near food poisoning incident which
resulted from an idiotic consumption of a spotted jelly corpse.  In
the top level of Sokoban, several remnants of orc corpses were found,
proving that he slayed as many as two dozen orcs.  His journal also
notes a conveyance of poison resistance, froma golden naga hatchling,
which later saved his life from a poisoned arrow shot.

Thereupon he descended into the dwarvish mines.  He came across a
ghost in minetown, and stocked up his bag of holding to the point
where he was burdened regardless.  The previous adventurer had a vast
array of wands, rings and scrolls.  Also included was a pair of
gloves, a pair of speed boots, and a large shield.  Wisely, he reduced
some of the load gathered by checking the b/u/c status at the
non-aligned altar.  At one point a few levels lower, his large dog
Sirius stepped onto a trap of polymorph, and thereby became the baby
blue dragon Smaug.  This good fortune was double teamed by Erik's
consumption of a floating eye corpse.  Oh, how well things were going.

Then it all went wrong.  Smaug met his end in the Dwarven King's mine
cellar, to the hands of a Minotaur.  We know this, because we pried
the journal of Erik from the bone pile of the said Minotaur.  Erik
died in the Dwarven King's mine cellar at the hands of the same
Minotaur, with a whole pack of wands and a bag of holding with many
scrolls.  He was Xlvl11, had an expert skill in dagger, and was valued
at 48161 zorkmids.  It's estimated that he spent 11,500 minutes in the
dungeon.

